{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_23b30b81b8025409e7b0705e222c0ec546ee7ef38befb2c4fb369a6ab493d941","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"doucs91/hivelore@f6ddcc78c4fe snapshot 84c09b59240bf4ba","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6cd29cf19c3ba6fc9ccff908d3a758ce8714876cd4178e3c06b065f3cab2bc77"],"source_ids":["src_94ce43533247585197669b2c74b96d8e"],"text":"Memory verbs mirror MCP tool names across CLI and MCP (save/search/get/delete ↔ mem_save/mem_search/mem_get/mem_delete), with older add/query/show/rm aliases still working.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2830a97721f29189e00c310e09a035f2e4e8cf1ea98d3e016367fdc1498aa979","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"doucs91/hivelore@f6ddcc78c4fe snapshot 84c09b59240bf4ba","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e6c670e1ab94c55da320338f9676f81c3735a4186a3e11900b5ba52a6eba1569"],"source_ids":["src_94ce43533247585197669b2c74b96d8e"],"text":"Only deterministic, code-bound evidence can block a commit (validated sensors, anchored anti-patterns, stale anchors on touched files); anchor, literal-token, and semantic matches are surfaced for review, never blocked.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_436e7356c3fad348111d274b9ad67c70d222a5eab4a9fdf37ea95f28a3098404","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"doucs91/hivelore@f6ddcc78c4fe snapshot 84c09b59240bf4ba","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1f1719a43c3a279450d0269cedce7a4a95ffd33f679ed632883c19cb0bce2b7e","slc_9014bdee60a00559e2b720f5d15e3123690c3a104c6823b65028102142314bc3"],"source_ids":["src_94ce43533247585197669b2c74b96d8e"],"text":"Since v0.57.0 anchor matches are weighted by path rarity (IDF): anchors touched by over 35% of recent commits need corroboration to outrank others, and too-small samples are reported as unknown and rank as before.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_55677261abc0c96447a1e50f5478317544b8dce488de4134b7a93de2b0b294ef","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"doucs91/hivelore@f6ddcc78c4fe snapshot 84c09b59240bf4ba","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_59aacbe53b94626dd7f21b42268c2055a9ef3a1a4865bf7e52b28e2d1b0dd5db","slc_fc7393e009f278359cd32bccc9fb6a781155f6618c69b5d4c0a46e80142a85ee"],"source_ids":["src_94ce43533247585197669b2c74b96d8e"],"text":"The monorepo contains @hivelore/cli (main product), @hivelore/mcp (bundled MCP server), @hivelore/core (types, schema, anchors, token budgets), @hivelore/embeddings (optional offline semantic ranking), plus a VS Code extension and a GitHub Action.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_57a8e60a48ec47a0d8a0be6b2b26906c6307de537130f9fb26695b6104e43f45","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"doucs91/hivelore@f6ddcc78c4fe snapshot 84c09b59240bf4ba","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_69ee1c7ba761d7794d5a2a337eff25e2f4033ba1c276d648e92fa92788efed23","slc_7fdb50fed31043ff4770679632d4e8feec51c1331e717c7854f8e257a29b0e0b","slc_b58d4928805cd5c42557eb722c119b384fd00437c0a7806a92dfaa227911ad4b","slc_dda2f7ff320b4c63e45a59ff04112587a7e07822cf1845a66d946ffc2079c8ef"],"source_ids":["src_94ce43533247585197669b2c74b96d8e"],"text":"Knowledge lives as Git-native Markdown records (decision, gotcha, convention, attempt, architecture) under .ai/, anchored to file paths and symbols; team memories are committed to git while personal memories and runtime/cache state are gitignored.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6ec40cca31ae0aa4f3a361ebc5d88e46217a9c900317949432e85a6102164831","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"doucs91/hivelore@f6ddcc78c4fe snapshot 84c09b59240bf4ba","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6d5bc6908ff9b89a41f9a0db85041ee91b8d6b0ea2784bf4e8333e69734d7185","slc_86ecb22cab8bc1ebcd12cd845c213b2a180a8292855926975d8959a64a0038f3","slc_c55773022699a128d363011de79ebd18dd9c60051adf1e5a93571779844f8f2b","slc_fc7393e009f278359cd32bccc9fb6a781155f6618c69b5d4c0a46e80142a85ee"],"source_ids":["src_94ce43533247585197669b2c74b96d8e"],"text":"The CLI requires Node >= 20 and is published as @hivelore/cli on npm; ast-grep sensors need the optional @ast-grep/napi engine, and semantic search needs the optional @hivelore/embeddings package (~110MB model).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7fb09af8086175b05cb6c0cff2194ef7542b4be1e47482e62fdc4513a347c201","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"doucs91/hivelore@f6ddcc78c4fe snapshot 84c09b59240bf4ba","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4d4d36bc792db45d94adca15bafaddcbbd7ead0751bbf526c68723641433a8d3","slc_ae0c4d76819b228acd93851ae852e7b2dbeb510816f86fc2b79e7c7a6c5a35b1"],"source_ids":["src_94ce43533247585197669b2c74b96d8e"],"text":"Sensors follow a validation doctrine of silent on correct code and firing on the mistake; autogenerated sensors start as warn and humans promote vetted ones to block, and inverted patterns matching the lesson's own fix are refused.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","created_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8ad5802dd396d693c5feb044e107703d819555a30dd71dda04a0c8568a6bfa98","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"doucs91/hivelore@f6ddcc78c4fe snapshot 84c09b59240bf4ba","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_951b338850102da763f74ddba239cc1f0dea9ad24201b71304128c38a96f493e","slc_efad2878882211360e21a065428dbcbe686f2caf59bac3e82dbd978dd421d9ad"],"source_ids":["src_94ce43533247585197669b2c74b96d8e"],"text":"Enforcement is governed by a single posture knob (advisory, balanced default, strict); process gates never refuse a local commit at any posture, and strict adds process gates at pre-push and CI.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:48:07Z","updated_by_operation":"op_24d5d3610e46405b9718b67f7d7a6b2b"}
